My condolences first, that must *really* hurt. I'm no UNIX expert, but I do
know that your problem is not a process gone wild; instead, the problem is that
the level files with your character name exist in the hack directory, and UNIX
recognizes this when you try to start a new game with the same name. So it 
doesn't overwrite the existing files. Until you find some wizard to fix your
game, use nethack -u <charname> to play with another name.

Is there a utility like Recover that rebuilds crashed games from the level files
for UNIX? There is for the Mac version. Worked for me.

Sorry about inaccuracies etc., I hope some UNIX guru gets them straightened out.

